{"date": "2026-10-17", "post_id": 1489582, "title": "3D 67P", "permalink": "https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-17-3d-67p/", "media_type": "image", "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/build-your-own-3d-glasses/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Put on your red/blue glasses</a> and float next to the jagged and double-lobed nucleus of Churyumov-Gerasimenko, also known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/67P/ Churyumov%E2%80%93Gerasimenko\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Comet 67P</a> . The stereo anaglyph was created by combining two images from the <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/?date=141016\">Rosetta spacecraft's</a> narrow angle OSIRIS camera <a href=\"https://rosetta-3dcomet.cnes.fr/?q=en/content/ anag-nac2015-07-25t062848742zid301397549500f22nac2015-07-25t063846772zid301397549400f22p1s63\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">taken on July 25, 2015</a> from a distance of 184 kilometers. Numerous jets are emanating from the small solar system world's active surface near its closest approach to the Sun. The larger lobe is around 4 kilometers in diameter, joined to a smaller, 2.5 kilometer diameter lobe by a narrow neck. Rosetta's mission to the comet ended in September 2016 when the spacecraft was commanded to a controlled impact with the comet's surface . Keep those 3D glasses on though. You can check out a <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02324\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"> catalog</a> of nearly 1400 stereo anaglyphs created from <a href=\"https://rosetta-3dcomet.cnes.fr/?q=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Rosetta image data on this website.</a><br><br><strong>Tomorrow's picture:</strong> open space<br>", "credit": "<a href=\"http://www.esa.int/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">ESA</a> , <a href=\"http://rosetta.esa.int/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Rosetta</a> , <a href=\"http://www.mps.mpg.de/en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">MPS</a> , OSIRIS - Stereo Anaglyph: <a href=\"https://rosetta-3dcomet.cnes.fr/?q=en/theteam\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Philippe Lamy and The Team</a>", "copyright": "<a href=\"http://www.esa.int/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">ESA</a> , <a href=\"http://rosetta.esa.int/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Rosetta</a> , <a href=\"http://www.mps.mpg.de/en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">MPS</a> , OSIRIS - Stereo Anaglyph: <a href=\"https://rosetta-3dcomet.cnes.fr/?q=en/theteam\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Philippe Lamy and The Team</a>", "alt": "Red/blue stereo anaglyph of comet 67P.", "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-17-3d-67p/", "hdurl": "https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/october/anaglyph-NAC_2015-07-25T06.28.48.742Z_lamy.jpg?w=2628&h=2418&fit=clip&crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint", "basic_html": "<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title> APOD: 2026 October 17 - 3D 67P</title>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-17-3d-67p/\">\n<!-- gsfc meta tags -->\n<meta name=\"orgcode\" content=\"661\">\n<meta name=\"rno\" content=\"Dana Bolles\">\n<meta name=\"content-owner\" content=\"Robert Nemiroff\">\n<meta name=\"webmaster\" content=\"Stephen.F.Fantasia.1\">\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Explanation: Put on your red/blue glasses and float next to the jagged and double-lobed nucleus of Churyumov-Gerasimenko, also known as Comet 67P . The stereo anaglyph was created by combining two images from the Rosetta spacecraft&#039;s narrow angle OSIRIS camera taken on July 25, 2015 from a distance of 184 kilometers. Numerous jets are emanating from the small solar system world&#039;s active surface near its closest approach to the Sun. The larger lobe is around 4 kilometers in diameter, joined to a smaller, 2.5 kilometer diameter lobe by a narrow neck. Rosetta&#039;s mission to the comet ended in September 2016 when the spacecraft was commanded to a controlled impact with the comet&#039;s surface . Keep those 3D glasses on though. You can check out a  catalog of nearly 1400 stereo anaglyphs created from Rosetta image data on this website.Tomorrow&#039;s picture: open space\">\n<!-- -->\n<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"3d 67p\">\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"3D 67P\">\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-17-3d-67p/\">\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"NASA Science\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/october/anaglyph-NAC_2015-07-25T06.28.48.742Z_lamy.jpg?w=2628&#038;h=2418&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:secure_url\" content=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/october/anaglyph-NAC_2015-07-25T06.28.48.742Z_lamy.jpg?w=2628&#038;h=2418&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:alt\" content=\"Red/blue stereo anaglyph of comet 67P.\">\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-10-17T00:05:00-04:00\">\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2026-10-14T17:11:06-04:00\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"3D 67P\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@NASA\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@NASA\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/october/anaglyph-NAC_2015-07-25T06.28.48.742Z_lamy.jpg?w=2628&#038;h=2418&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\">\n</head>\n<body BGCOLOR=\"#F4F4FF\" text=\"#000000\" link=\"#0000FF\" vlink=\"#7F0F9F\"\nalink=\"#FF0000\">\n\n<center>\n<h1> Astronomy Picture of the Day </h1>\n<p>\n\n<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a>\nEach day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is\nfeatured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer.\n<p>\n\n2026 October 17<br>\n\n<a href=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/october/anaglyph-NAC_2015-07-25T06.28.48.742Z_lamy.jpg\">\n<IMG SRC=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/october/anaglyph-NAC_2015-07-25T06.28.48.742Z_lamy.jpg\" alt=\"Red/blue stereo anaglyph of comet 67P.\"></a>\n</center>\n\n<center>\n<b> 3D 67P </b> <br>\n\n<b>Image Credit &\n<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/about-apod/\">Copyright</a>:</b>\n\n<a href=\"http://www.esa.int/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">ESA</a> , <a href=\"http://rosetta.esa.int/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Rosetta</a> , <a href=\"http://www.mps.mpg.de/en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">MPS</a> , OSIRIS - Stereo Anaglyph: <a href=\"https://rosetta-3dcomet.cnes.fr/?q=en/theteam\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Philippe Lamy and The Team</a>\n</center>\n\n<p>\n\n<b> Explanation: </b>\n\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/build-your-own-3d-glasses/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Put on your red/blue glasses</a> and float next to the jagged and double-lobed nucleus of Churyumov-Gerasimenko, also known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/67P/ Churyumov%E2%80%93Gerasimenko\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Comet 67P</a> . The stereo anaglyph was created by combining two images from the <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/?date=141016\">Rosetta spacecraft's</a> narrow angle OSIRIS camera <a href=\"https://rosetta-3dcomet.cnes.fr/?q=en/content/ anag-nac2015-07-25t062848742zid301397549500f22nac2015-07-25t063846772zid301397549400f22p1s63\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">taken on July 25, 2015</a> from a distance of 184 kilometers. Numerous jets are emanating from the small solar system world's active surface near its closest approach to the Sun. The larger lobe is around 4 kilometers in diameter, joined to a smaller, 2.5 kilometer diameter lobe by a narrow neck. Rosetta's mission to the comet ended in September 2016 when the spacecraft was commanded to a controlled impact with the comet's surface . Keep those 3D glasses on though. You can check out a <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02324\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"> catalog</a> of nearly 1400 stereo anaglyphs created from <a href=\"https://rosetta-3dcomet.cnes.fr/?q=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Rosetta image data on this website.</a><br><br><strong>Tomorrow's picture:</strong> open space<br>\n<p> <center>\n\n\n<p> <hr>\n<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-16-chasing-the-international-space-station/\">&lt;</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Archive</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Index</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Search</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/calendar/\">Calendar</a>\n| <a href=\"/feed/apod-basic/\">RSS</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/education-links/\">Education</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/about-apod/\">About APOD</a>\n| &gt;\n\n<hr><p>\n<b> Authors & editors: </b>\nJerry Bonnell, Cecilia Chirenti, Robert Nemiroff, Keighley Rockcliffe<br>\n<b>NASA Official: </b> Dana Bolles<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/about-apod/\">Specific rights apply</a>.<br>\n<a href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/about/highlights/HP_Privacy.html\">NASA Web\nPrivacy Policy and Important Notices</a><br>\n<b>A service of:</b>\n<a href=\"http://astrophysics.gsfc.nasa.gov/\">ASD</a> at\n<a href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/\">NASA</a> /\n<a href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/centers/goddard/\">GSFC</a>\n<br><b>&</b> <a href=\"http://www.mtu.edu/\">Michigan Tech. U.</a><br>\n</center>\n</body>\n</html>", "basic_html_url": "https://science.nasa.gov/wp-json/wp/v2/apod-basic/261017/html"}